rebuild-history-projections-from-paginated-rollouts

Lane: backend

Unit: rebuild-sqlite-history-from-paginated-rollouts

ChildPatch: rebuild-history-projections-from-paginated-rollouts

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Rebuild SQLite history and recover indexed session titles after database loss without rewriting already-paginated rollouts.

Requires: Unit:normalization/route-thread-writer-locks-to-harness

Provides: Manual migrate-rollouts apply rebuilds projections under native writer locks, reconciles missing metadata, cleans compressed staging, preserves immutable rollout identities, and prunes stale names after a complete successful scan; startup backfill restores indexed names into missing rows while preserving existing SQLite names and explicit clears.

Boundary: The name index remains under CODEX_HOME; dry runs, legacy canonicalization, rollout formats, database schemas, locking and rate limiting retain native ownership. Unreadable manual indexes fail explicitly and startup backfill remains unfinished.

Verification: local::rollout_migration::tests cover database-loss recovery, compressed preservation, idempotence and scoped pruning; metadata::tests cover active and archived title recovery, existing SQLite names, explicit clears and unreadable-index backfill.


